@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
@prefix sulo: <https://w3id.org/sulo/> .
@prefix obo: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .

# Adapted from the SULO paper's Figure 7 (the PRO pattern), NOT
# transcribed verbatim: the paper's own listing is not valid Turtle
# and would not parse as printed. Repairs applied, all recorded in
# spec 9.1 and in ../README.md:
#   - namespace corrected from http://w3id.org/sulo/ to
#     https://w3id.org/sulo/
#   - the missing terminating dot on @prefix obo:, and the stray dot
#     that orphaned the sulo:hasParticipant line, both fixed
#   - taxon: is not used here (obo:NCBITaxon_9606 used directly
#     instead, which the paper's own inference example also uses)
#   - the inferred subject renamed from :visit_1 to :encounter, to
#     match the individual the data itself defines
#   - the two role individuals are typed sulo:Role EXPLICITLY. The
#     paper types them only as OMRSE classes (OMRSE_00000011,
#     OMRSE_00000012), which are not imported into sulo.ttl, so
#     nothing makes them sulo:Role and the property chain cannot fire
#     as printed. This is a substantive repair, not a typo.

ex:encounter a sulo:Process .

ex:alice a obo:NCBITaxon_9606, sulo:Object .
ex:drsmith a obo:NCBITaxon_9606, sulo:Object .

ex:patient-role a sulo:Role ;
    sulo:isFeatureOf ex:alice .

ex:doctor-role a sulo:Role ;
    sulo:isFeatureOf ex:drsmith .

ex:encounter sulo:hasParticipant ex:patient-role, ex:doctor-role .
